## Use Case for eu-ehds:DataPermit
Description: This example illustrates the formal legal authorisation required for post-market Drug Safety Monitoring, which is a high-priority 
secondary use category under the EHDS. It centers on a use case where a National Medicines Agency must investigate an unexpected side effect linked to 
a specific cardiovascular medication by analysing health data across multiple regions. Because this involves processing sensitive clinical records 
for a regulatory purpose rather than individual patient care, it requires a Data Permit issued by a Health Data Access Body (HDAB) under EHDS 
Article 68. The data permit acts as the formal Organisational Measure that provides the Official Authority to access the data. It identifies the 
Medicines Agency as the authorised recipient and strictly limits the processing to Public Health Monitoring activities within the health sector. 
Modeling this as a eu-ehds:DataPermit, the framework ensures the data remains within a Secure Processing Environment (SPE) and is used only for 
the time-bound duration of the safety investigation. The metadata includes the authorisation of the Medicines Agency, the specific legal basis 
under GDPR Art. 6(1)(e), and the requirement for a protected environment, providing a machine-readable guarantee that the agency’s access is 
strictly limited to the necessary window for ensuring public safety.
